rankin@pactechdata.com wrote:
> On Oct 8, 11:26 am, rpresser <rpres...@gmail.com> wrote:
>> The patch I'm thinking of would allow multiple bones files to be saved
>> for each level.
>> [...]
>> It doesn't seem technically too difficult to implement. Is it too
>> meaningless to worry about?
> 
>      I suspect that it'll be harder than you think.  Some of
> the platforms don't provide a supported way to do wildcarded
> file lookup, so you'd need to step through each possible file
> name looking for one that exists, or else rename the remainder
> after consuming one from the front or middle of the list.

Well, I think this should be a solvable problem from an algorithmic 
point of view; for instance, append _n to the filename where n goes from 
1 to the number of bones for this level.

Using a binary search one should be able to quickly determine this n (as 
needed for saving and loading the way I suggest).  When loading, always 
load the *last* bones file (shouldn't cause any problems, should it?), 
so the sequence of numbers n is always continuous.

The only possible problem here should be race-conditions again, it is 
necessary to synchronize saving a bones file and loading one by a 
seperate process, so deleting the loaded one does not cause holes in 
this number-sequence.

